---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';
import CardGrid from '../../components/CardGrid.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Implementation"
  description="The UniDPP open reference implementation: unidpp-core (Rust), unidpp-ts, unidpp-rb, unidpp-py, resolver, signatif, and explorer — with conformance fixtures derived from the full converted corpus."
  eyebrow="04 · Reference — implementation"
>
  <h1>Implementation</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A fully open, multi-language implementation of the framework, developed in the open
    under Apache-2.0 / MIT. Conformance fixtures are derived from the full converted corpus
    of the EN series, the CEN Workshop Agreements, and the IDTA specifications — including
    the published defect registers as negative test cases.
  </p>

  <section id="repositories" class="plate" aria-labelledby="repos-h">
    <h2 id="repos-h">Repositories</h2>
    <CardGrid>
      <Card title="unidpp-core" tag="Rust">
        <p>
          The canonical model and algorithms. Modules: <code>identity</code>
          (scheme-agnostic IDs; ISO/IEC 15459 parsing and bridging);
          <code>model</code> (core passport, manifest, PassportLink edges);
          <code>event</code> (typed events, append-only log, commitment hashing);
          <code>transform</code> (split/combine with mass balance and taint propagation);
          <code>tier_a</code> (offline packer: minimum fields, multi-suite signature
          framing, carrier-size budgeting); <code>verdict</code> (graded trust, coverage
          reports, freshness); <code>resolver</code> (linkset emission and parsing, context
          routing). Property tests: quantity conservation, commitment consistency,
          casing-normalization conformance.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="unidpp-ts" tag="npm @unidpp/*">
        <p>
          Types generated from the unidpp-spec JSON Schema; client for the resolver,
          registry, and passport APIs; validators; runs in browsers, including an in-browser
          Tier-A verification demonstration.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="unidpp-rb" tag="gem unidpp">
        <p>
          Registry client (FERIN / ISO 19135 items, statuses, supersession); glossarist
          bridge between terminology and registry anchors; expressir/CDDAL hooks for schema
          validation; CNML/ESDC handling via lutaml-model.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="unidpp-py" tag="PyPI unidpp">
        <p>
          Verification-pipeline harness driving unidpp-core via FFI/CLI; conformance
          runners over the positive corpus and the audit-derived negative cases; adapters
          for UNTP, EPCIS, and GS1 Digital Link; paper and tooling glue.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="unidpp-spec" tag="specification">
        <p>
          The JSON Schema and EXPRESS sources from which SDK types, validators, and
          conformance suites are generated. The specification is the single source; SDKs
          are renders.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="unidpp-resolver" tag="resolution">
        <p>
          Federated resolution with linkset routing by profile context, role, language, and
          request region; dark identities that never enter the global resolver.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="unidpp-signatif" tag="trust">
        <p>
          Trust path-finding on the SIGNATIF model; root and master-list threshold
          ceremonies on Confium quorum operations.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="unidpp-explorer" tag="inspection">
        <p>
          Inspection of passports, event logs, manifests, and verdicts; entry point for
          conformance reporting on the fixture corpus.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </CardGrid>
  </section>

  <section id="quickstart" aria-labelledby="quickstart-h">
    <h2 id="quickstart-h">Quickstart</h2>
    <p>Language SDKs install from their registries:</p>
    <pre><code># Rust (core algorithms)
cargo add unidpp-core
# TypeScript (client, validators — generated types included)
npm install @unidpp/client @unidpp/validators
# Ruby (registry client, glossarist bridge)
gem install unidpp
# Python (verification pipeline, conformance runners)
pip install unidpp</code></pre>
    <p>To build the core from source:</p>
    <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/unidpp/unidpp-core
cd unidpp-core
cargo build --release
cargo test            # property tests: quantity conservation, commitment consistency</code></pre>
    <div class="note">
      Initial releases are staged as each repository reaches its first tagged version; the
      module decomposition above is the committed set. Repositories are published under
      the <a href="https://github.com/unidpp">unidpp</a> GitHub organization.
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
